A||||8||Mark Matthews||Will these tires work?||||5||
Z||000000||Mark Matthews||12-07-2001||10:07 AM||||Well, I'm gonna change all the tires, but I have 195/50-R15 tires sitting in my garage.  Will these work or is that too small?  Right now 215/60-R15's on the car.  Thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!  ;)||||reg||5
Z||000001||WampusCat||12-07-2001||11:09 AM||||The circumference of the 215/60's is 79".  The 195/50 are only 71.2" around.  That's about an 10% difference so your engine will rev 10% higher to cruise at the same speed and speedometer will indicate 10% faster than you are actually going.  Plus there will be a larger gap between tire and fender because the 195's are about 2.5" shorter than the 215's and they won't look as cool.  But yes they will work.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark Matthews||12-07-2001||11:25 AM||||Decided against it, thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Mark Matthews<BR>'57 Chevy BelAir<BR>'70 BMW 2002<BR>'87 GT Fastback T-top<BR>'96 4x4 Tahoe<BR>'74 Wife, not happy about cars!  ;)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black86SE||12-08-2001||04:13 PM||||I though that the bigger the tires, the faster the speedo shows. That is the problem with my truck. I can run 72 mph on my speedo and I am actually going like 80 mph.||||reg||1
