Z||000005||BlackARROW||12-12-2001||06:22 PM||||Just to bring some extra info for TireSize freaks:<P>If the width is lowered, the ratio for the thickness is raised, it should not be lowered too. You got to keep the same circonference. 215/60 should become 195/65.<P>If you keep the same wheel diameter (in this case 15) you can go with this approach:<P>w * r = W * R  (215 * 0.6 = 195 * ?)<P>It gives 0.66, so a ratio of 65 on 195 would work not so bad, but not less.  But I think these 65 are harder to find than 185/70 - which gives a 0.697 related to your 215/60)<P>But if you change the wheel diameter, like on a mag upgrade  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> you have to go with the big stuff.<P>c = (2 * (w * r) / 25.4) + d) * pi<BR>     c : circonference<BR>     w : width<BR>     r : ratio<BR>     d : wheel diameter<BR>     25.4 is to convert "mm" into "inches"<P>Let's suppose that your topspeed with 215/60r15 is 120mph at 4500rpm, well with your 195/50r15 at 4500rpm, you will go at about 108.165mph (just about).  Big difference eh?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Formula:<BR>r = (s * 63,360) / c<BR>    r : number of revolution<BR>    s : speed in mph<BR>    c : circonference of the wheel in inches<BR>** Of course, this formula assume your tire is fully inflated :P  hehe..<P>Don't overload your calculator with all this crap.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>You could go to this webpage, if you prefer graphical stuff: <A HREF="http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html</A> <P>Black--&gt;<BR>Fiero 2m4 '85<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||12-13-2001||12:41 AM||||Buying budget tyres is like breathing budget air...<P>Get a good set of NEW OE size rubber.<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
